            <ArticleTitle>Evidence for homologous actions of pro-opiocortin products.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1247-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>alpha-Melanocyte-stimulating hormone (alpha-MSH), a modified fragment of adrenocorticotropic hormone, derives from the same biosynthetic route as beta-endorphin and is stored by the same arcuate neurons. Microinjection of alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone and several related peptides into the periaqueductal gray matter significantly reduced responsiveness to pain and had a behavioral profile similar to that produced by beta-endorphin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
